      "message": "test(adaptive): re-measure the STEP bore's heavy Adaptive pin after #839\n\nPR #839 (merge 575f02d8) caps the STEP chord at 0.005 mm, so the user's\nbore in Milling-test.step is meshed far finer; on the new outline the\nZ 10 level's HSM plan crosses itself and Offset rings cut it, as Z 20\nalready did. Measured: 575f02d8^1 passes (Z 20 only, 5530/5497/600);\n575f02d8 and main f490458a give Z 20 + Z 10, 6500/6464/222, warnings\nempty. The pin now asserts exactly {Z 20, Z 10}, each \"crosses itself\",\nand 6500/6464/222; every safety assertion is unchanged. Three release\nruns identical. Getting the Z 10 plan back is #980 part 2.\n\nRefs #980\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
